name: sim.getObjectFromUid
description: Retrieves an object handle based on its unique identifier
luaSynopsis: int objectHandle = sim.getObjectFromUid(int objectUid, dict options = {})
pythonSynopsis: int objectHandle = sim.getObjectFromUid(int objectUid, table options = {})
inputs:
1. objectUid: the object unique identifier.
2. options: optional map indicating how the object should be searched. {noError=true} will generate a silent error if an object was not found.
outputs:
1. objectHandle: handle of object
